+# Storage Conditions Product Field Design
+
+## Purpose
+
+Merchants need to record handling instructions such as "Keep refrigerated at
+2–8 °C" for individual products. Staff must manage the value and its
+translations in the Dashboard. Customers must see the effective localized
+value on the storefront product detail page.
+
+The field is optional, plain text, and limited to 250 characters. It is not
+shown in product listings, carts, checkout, or order communications.
+
+It is included in product webhook payloads and product CSV exports. Product
+CSV import, API filters, and search do not support the field.
+
+## Data Model
+
+Add `storage_conditions` to both `Product` and `ProductTranslation`:
+
+- `Product.storage_conditions` is the canonical, nullable text value with a
+  maximum length of 250 characters.
+- `ProductTranslation.storage_conditions` is the nullable, per-language
+  override with the same limit.
+- Empty and `null` values mean no value at that level.
+
+A Django migration adds both columns. Existing products remain valid and
+display no new block until a canonical or translated value is set.
+
+## GraphQL API
+
+Expose the field through Saleor's normal product API:
+
+- Add it to the `Product` type and to `Product.translation(languageCode:)`.
+- Add it to `ProductInput` for product create and update.
+- Add it to the product translation input and translation mutation payload.
+- Enforce the 250-character limit through Django and GraphQL validation.
+- Continue to use the existing `MANAGE_PRODUCTS` permission for writes.
+
+The storefront product query requests the canonical field and the active
+locale's translation. It resolves an effective value by using a non-empty
+translation first and otherwise the canonical value. An empty translation
+therefore clears that locale's override rather than suppressing the canonical
+value.
+
+## Dashboard
+
+Add an optional single-line **Storage conditions** field to the existing
+product details form. It loads and saves the canonical value through the
+standard create/update path.
+
+Add the same optional field to the existing product translation editor. Saving
+stores a locale-specific override; clearing it removes the override so
+storefronts use the canonical value. The Dashboard enforces a 250-character
+input limit and relies on the API as the authoritative validation layer.
+
+The work reuses existing product form state, GraphQL generation, localized
+messages, save notifications, and error handling. It introduces no new
+permissions, routes, or dependencies.
+
+## Storefront
+
+Extend only the product detail query, cached product shell, and product-view
+mapping with the effective storage-condition value. Do not add the field to
+listing, cart, checkout, or order queries.
+
+On the product detail page, render a separate semantic block directly after
+the product description:
+
+- The block uses a code-owned, `next-intl`-translated label: "Storage
+  conditions".
+- The plain-text value is rendered as React text.
+- The block is not rendered when the effective value is empty.
+
+The block belongs in the product description area, rather than the
+specification/attribute section or purchase controls.
+
+## Error Handling and Compatibility
+
+Invalid overlength values follow Saleor's standard mutation validation and
+Dashboard error presentation. Storefronts keep the product page functional if
+the field is absent or empty, as is the case for all existing products.
+
+The product's existing invalidation flow applies after updates. The storefront
+uses the existing product cache profile and product-update invalidation, so a
+changed value becomes visible through the same mechanism as product
+description changes.
+
+## Outbound Integrations
+
+Product webhook subscription payloads expose the canonical
+`storageConditions` field through the product selection. Translation-aware
+subscriptions can select the localized value through the product translation
+selection using the same fallback decisions as other product fields.
+
+Product CSV export adds a **Storage conditions** column containing the
+canonical value. Empty values export as blank cells. CSV import is unchanged:
+it neither accepts nor updates storage conditions.
+
+The field is not added to product filters, search indexes, or search
+documents.
+
+## Local Development Migration
+
+Apply the existing Django migration only to the local development database.
+Restart the local API after migration so the updated GraphQL schema and
+webhook subscription contract are served. No production deployment or data
+backfill is part of this work.
+
+## Testing
+
+Backend coverage verifies:
+
+- Product create and update save canonical values.
+- Product translation writes and reads localized values.
+- Product query and translation query expose the values.
+- The 250-character boundary succeeds and longer input returns validation
+  errors.
+- Empty and `null` values are accepted.
+- Existing product permissions remain enforced.
+
+Dashboard coverage verifies canonical and translation form initialization,
+submission, clearing, input limits, and mutation errors.
+
+Storefront coverage verifies canonical display, locale override, fallback for
+missing or empty translations, and omission of the block when no effective
+value exists. It also verifies that the PDP-only query and mapper changes do
+not add the field to cart, checkout, or order flows.
+
+Webhook coverage verifies product subscription queries can select the
+canonical field. CSV coverage verifies the export header and row value,
+including blank output for empty values. Tests verify that import, filters,
+and search remain unchanged.
+
+Run the smallest relevant backend, Dashboard, and storefront tests, followed
+by each repository's targeted type generation, lint, and type-check commands.
